          <p>
            ISO100 in the 5 lb tub, about 70 servings, typically works out to roughly $1.30 to $1.70 per 25 g. That is fair for a tested isolate. Most certified isolates land between $1.30 and $2.00, and premium grass-fed isolates often cost more. Small 1.3 lb tubs cost more per gram, so buy big once you know you like a flavor.
          </p>

          <p>
            Elite 100% Whey usually lands at roughly $1.00 to $1.25 per 25 g in the 5 lb size, which puts it among the cheaper tested wheys on the market. Elite Casein, sold in 4 lb tubs, typically sits between the two. For the cheapest options overall, see our <a href="/best-cheap-protein-powder/">best cheap protein powder</a> guide.
          </p>

          <p>
            Over a year of one shake a day, the gap between ISO100 and Elite Whey is often $100 or more. That is real money for a benefit, lower lactose, that many people do not need. Try Elite Whey first unless you already know dairy bothers you.
          </p>
