              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the difference between Dymatize ISO100 and Elite Whey?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Both give about 25 g of protein per scoop. ISO100 is all whey isolate, partly hydrolyzed, with very little lactose and about 110 to 120 calories. Elite Whey blends concentrate, isolate and peptides and runs about 140 calories with more lactose. Elite Whey usually costs 20 to 30 percent less per 25 g. Choose ISO100 for dairy sensitivity or strict cuts.
