              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Not technically, but it is very low in lactose. Whey isolate is filtered to remove most lactose, and ISO100 typically lists under 1 to 2 g of sugar per scoop. Many people who react to regular whey tolerate it well. People with a milk allergy, which is a reaction to milk protein rather than lactose, should avoid it entirely.
              </p>
